RollingEPUB
Copyright (c) 2026 RollingEPUB contributors

This library merges the EPUB parsing/rendering work of two independent reader
projects. Portions of the source are adapted from the projects below, under
their respective licenses. All adapted files carry an SPDX header and a
provenance comment naming the origin.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. RollingEPUB original code
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MIT License. See licenses/MIT.txt.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. CrossSIGO / CrossMux
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Upstream: https://github.com/0x1abin/crossmux (CrossPoint Reader fork)
License: MIT
Copyright (c) 2025 Dave Allie
Copyright (c) 2026 FreeInk
Copyright (c) 2026 EEGO A4 Template Firmware contributors
Copyright (c) 2025 CrossPoint Reader organization

Adapted areas:
  * CSS cascade model and selector matching (lib/Epub/Epub/css)
  * HTML entity table (lib/Epub/Epub/htmlEntities)
  * OPF/NCX/NAV parser structure and metadata model (lib/Epub/Epub/parsers,
    Epub.cpp)
  * Page/section model concepts: anchors, visible-text offsets, page links
    (lib/Epub/Epub/Section.*, Page.*)
  * Liang hyphenation algorithm and English pattern data
    (lib/Epub/Epub/hyphenation)
  * Image dithering / 1-2 bit conversion concepts (lib/Epub/Epub/converters)
  * ZIP container conventions (lib/ZipFile, lib/miniz)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Read Pico / kiikoread
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Upstream: https://github.com/wegooo-cell/read-pico-reader
License of reused files: Apache-2.0 (SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 in the
source headers), copyright (c) 2026 mindreset and contributors.
Full license text: licenses/Apache-2.0.txt.

Adapted areas:
  * ZIP entry access policy and bounds (main/book/zip_reader.c)
  * OPF/spine/cover/navigation pipeline and byte-weighted progress
    (main/book/book_epub.c)
  * HTML -> text/blocks state machine, CSS subset, footnote extraction,
    anchor mapping (main/book/html_text.c)
  * Pixel pagination, CJK line breaking/kinsoku, vertical writing, image and
    footnote placement (main/book/book_layout.c)
  * TTF glyph cache / vertical drawing / coverage-level concepts
    (main/font/ttf_font.c)
  * Image header dimension probing (main/book/book_image_header.c)

NOTE: Read Pico also contains files marked
`SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-Kiikoread-Personal-Study-1.0`
(non-commercial). RollingEPUB does NOT copy code from those files. Only files
whose headers declare Apache-2.0 (or that predate the policy change and remain
Apache-2.0 per the repository LICENSE scope) are reused.

